# CVE-2026-33671 — picomatch 4.0.3 ReDoS.
# Present ONLY in the npm CLI bundled with the node:22-slim base image
# (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/picomatch), not in our app deps
# (we pin picomatch >=4.0.4 via package.json overrides). npm is not invoked at
# runtime — the production image runs `node dist/src/main.js` — so this code path
# is not reachable. Will clear when the base image ships a patched npm.
CVE-2026-33671

# CVE-2026-48815 — @sigstore/* certificateOIDs verification bypass.
# Same situation as above: present ONLY in the npm CLI bundled with the
# node:22-slim base image (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/@sigstore),
# not in our app deps (our lockfile has no sigstore). npm's package-provenance
# verification is not invoked at runtime, so this code path is not reachable.
# Will clear when the base image ships a patched npm.
CVE-2026-48815

# CVE-2026-14257 — brace-expansion 5.0.7 ReDoS.
# Present ONLY in the npm CLI bundled with the node:22-slim base image
# (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/brace-expansion). Our own app deps
# are patched — the lockfile pins the 5.0.x copies to 5.0.8 and every copy is a
# devDependency pruned out of the production image (`npm prune --omit=dev`). npm is
# not invoked at runtime — the image runs `node dist/src/main.js` — and the offline
# `npx prisma migrate deploy` path passes no attacker-controlled brace patterns, so
# the ReDoS is not reachable. Will clear when the base image ships a patched npm.
CVE-2026-14257

# CVE-2026-69152 — brace-expansion DoS via unbounded intermediate arrays.
# Same base-image situation as CVE-2026-14257 above: the flagged 5.0.7 copy ships
# ONLY inside the npm CLI bundled with node:22-slim
# (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/brace-expansion). Our own app deps
# are clear — the lockfile now pins every 5.0.x copy to 5.0.9 (fixed) via the
# `brace-expansion@5` override, and the remaining 1.x/2.x copies are devDependencies
# pruned out of the production image (`npm prune --omit=dev`). npm is not invoked at
# runtime — the image runs `node dist/src/main.js` — so the vulnerable code path is
# not reachable. Will clear when the base image ships a patched npm.
CVE-2026-69152
